  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Derived, never stored",
      "items": [
        "There is no status column: derive_status() in backend/storage/journeys.py reads five dates on job_journeys plus job_interviews.scheduled_at",
        "The API returns status read-only; PATCH /api/journeys/{id} accepts dates only",
        "job_feedback.outcome is snapshotted from the same function as the row is written, never passed in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "First match wins",
      "items": [
        "derive_status() tries the rungs in one fixed order: rejected, offer, dropped, on_hold, in_progress, applied or silent, draft",
        "rejected_at is terminal — no lower rung is consulted, whatever the other dates say",
        "rejected_at, offer_at and dropped_at can be written from any live state, not only the ones drawn here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "One rung reads the clock",
      "items": [
        "silent needs no write: applied plus quiet_after_days (settings.json, default 30) of nothing flips it overnight",
        "Every test asserting a status must pass now=, or it goes stale as its fixtures age",
        "Only the employer resets the clock — last_contact_at() counts rounds and feedback, never events, because a follow-up you sent is not a reply"
      ]
    }
  ]
}